            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Patient Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>
                    Patient management can become difficult when information is fragmented, processes are manual, or communication is inconsistent. Digital workflows can help address these challenges.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Fragmented Patient Information: Bring relevant patient information together in a structured environment for authorized access.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Missed Appointments: Use automated reminders and communication workflows to improve appointment awareness and follow-up.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Manual Data Entry: Reduce repetitive entry through workflow automation and integrations where appropriate.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Limited Patient Communication: Provide consistent notifications, reminders, and communication channels to keep patients informed.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Poor Follow-Up Visibility: Use task management, alerts, and dashboards to help teams track outstanding patient-related activities.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />
                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Patient Management</b></h3>
                <p>Patient services vary across hospitals, clinics, diagnostic centers, and specialty providers. Customization helps digital solutions reflect each organization's patient workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Customize Patient Workflows: Configure workflows around registration, scheduling, communication, follow-up, and service requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Role-Based Experiences: Provide relevant functionality for administrators, clinicians, support teams, and other authorized users.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automate Patient Communications: Create tailored reminders, notifications, and follow-up workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Build Patient-Focused Dashboards: Give teams visibility into appointments, activities, follow-ups, and operational performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Use Feedback to Improve: Gather feedback from staff and patients to continuously improve the digital experience.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
